hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1512","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: Amr bin Salamah told us. H Abu Hashim Ziyad bin Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Salamah, he said: We were present, so it was The riders passed by us, returning from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I approached them and listened until I memorized the Qur’an. He said: The people were waiting with their conversion to Islam for the conquest of Mecca, and when it was opened, a man began to come to him and say: O Messenger of God, I am the arrival of the tribe of so-and-so. I brought you their conversion to Islam, so my father set out to convert his people to Islam. When he returned, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Present most of them.” “Quran.” He said: So they looked, and I am on Eve. Al-Dawrqi said: Eve is great, and Abu Hashim said: Eve, and they said: They did not find anyone among them who had more recited the Qur’an. From me, so they brought me forward while I was a boy, so I prayed with them, and I was wearing a cloak of mine, so whenever I bowed or prostrated, my private parts would be exposed, so when we prayed, you would say to us Eternal old women: Cover us, your reader. He said: They cut a shirt for me. He said: I think so. He said: From the location of the two rivers, and he mentioned that he was very happy with it. Al-Dawraqi said: He said: “The one who recites the Qur’an the most among you will lead you in prayer.”"
